WEBVTT

00:00:00.250 --> 00:00:02.550
Here we ask the agent which ATLAS techniques

00:00:02.550 --> 00:00:05.050
have no mitigations that satisfy
any ISO controls

00:00:05.380 --> 00:00:08.850
This is a question inquiring about the gaps
in our knowledge graph representation

00:00:09.260 --> 00:00:13.120
The agent will first get the schema
to learn about the knowledge graph,

00:00:13.340 --> 00:00:16.700
then correctly calls
an audit compliance gaps tool

00:00:17.100 --> 00:00:19.740
that traverses the graph for any gaps

00:00:20.420 --> 00:00:25.100
The agent correctly states that there are
109 techniques that are not mitigated,

00:00:27.550 --> 00:00:29.780
and states here the query used

00:00:32.100 --> 00:00:35.550
If we move on to the graph
to more intuitively understand what this means,

00:00:36.850 --> 00:00:40.650
there are ISO requirement nodes
like “AI risk assessment process”

00:00:40.700 --> 00:00:43.550
that mandate an ISO control

00:00:43.850 --> 00:00:48.950
The ISO control is connected to a mitigation
that satisfies that control

00:00:50.650 --> 00:00:53.650
The mitigation mitigates some technique

00:00:54.000 --> 00:00:56.150
We have a complete chain

00:00:57.050 --> 00:01:00.550
But there are some techniques
that have no connections

00:01:00.550 --> 00:01:03.650
to mitigations connected to ISO controls

00:01:03.650 --> 00:01:08.100
So there are some techniques which have
not been taken into account as risk scenarios

00:01:08.350 --> 00:01:11.100
If we run the query stated by the agent here,

00:01:12.500 --> 00:01:17.180
one of the techniques here is
“Obtain Capabilities,” which has ID 16
